# Go user environment snippet generated by infrastructure/mirrors/apply.sh
#
# GOPROXY is a comma-separated fallback chain. Go tries entries in order and
# falls through only for 404/410 responses. The `|` separator falls through on
# ANY error, including timeouts/5xx, which is what we need when the Bangladesh
# mirror is temporarily unavailable.
#
# Variables resolved at apply time:
#   MIRROR_GO_URL — regional Athens URL
#   GO_UPSTREAM   — upstream module proxy (default https://proxy.golang.org)
#
# The generated command is:
#   go env -w GOPROXY="${MIRROR_GO_URL}|${GO_UPSTREAM}|direct"
#   go env -w GOSUMDB="sum.golang.org"
#
# Security:
#   - GOSUMDB stays enabled to verify module checksums even through the mirror.
#   - `direct` is last because VCS clones are much heavier on bandwidth.
#   - Never set GOPRIVATE in a checked-in file; it can reveal internal module
#     names. Set it only in the user's private environment.
GOPROXY=${MIRROR_GO_URL}|${GO_UPSTREAM}|direct
GOSUMDB=sum.golang.org
